{"id":"motorcycle-diaries","title":"The Motorcycle Diaries","who":"Ernesto \"Che\" Guevara & Alberto Granado","when":"January–July 1952","vehicle":"1939 Norton 500 \"La Poderosa II\"","kind":"moto","color":"#4d7c0f","summary":"Two young Argentines set off from Buenos Aires on an old Norton to see the continent. The bike died in Chile; they carried on by truck, ship, raft and plane through the Andes, the Atacama, Machu Picchu and the Amazon, a trip that changed one of them for ever.","sources":[{"label":"Wikipedia: The Motorcycle Diaries (book)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Motorcycle_Diaries_(book)"}],"approximate":"Places follow the diary and later accounts; the roads of 1952 are drawn on today's roads.","km":11816,"bbox":[-77.3352,-41.1336,-57.5763,10.5065],"stops":[{"name":"Buenos Aires","place":"Buenos Aires, Argentina","at":[-34.6096,-58.3888],"date":"Jan 1952","text":"The start on La Poderosa II (\"the Mighty One\"), a 1939 Norton 500 loaded far beyond reason.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Puerto_Madero%2C_Buenos_Aires_%2840689219792%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Puerto_Madero%2C_Buenos_Aires_%2840689219792%29_%28cropped%29.jpg","page":"Buenos Aires","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Puerto_Madero%2C_Buenos_Aires_%2840689219792%29_%28cropped%29.jpg","credit":"Deensel","license":"CC BY 2.0"}},{"name":"Miramar","place":"Miramar, Buenos Aires","at":[-38.2704,-57.8388],"text":"A seaside stop to see Ernesto's girlfriend Chichina. Two days became eight."},{"name":"Bahía Blanca","place":"Bahía Blanca, Argentina","at":[-38.7177,-62.2655],"text":"South-west across the pampas, with falls and repairs along the way.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Vistas_de_Bahia_Blanca_%2824%29.jpg/500px-Vistas_de_Bahia_Blanca_%2824%29.jpg","page":"Bahía Blanca","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vistas_de_Bahia_Blanca_%2824%29.jpg","credit":"Juan Corral (Fotógrafo, Subdirección de Prensa y Contenidos Públicos del Municipio de Bahía Blanca)","license":"CC BY 2.5 ar"}},{"name":"Choele Choel","place":"Choele Choel, Argentina","at":[-39.2932,-65.6616],"text":"Ernesto fell ill with fever and spent days in hospital here.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Choele_acceso.jpg/500px-Choele_acceso.jpg","page":"Choele Choel","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Choele_acceso.jpg","credit":"Jorge Gustavo Silva","license":"CC0"}},{"name":"San Martín de los Andes","place":"San Martín de los Andes, Argentina","at":[-40.1569,-71.3526],"text":"Lakes and forests at the foot of the Andes.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/CPCpanoramica2.JPG/500px-CPCpanoramica2.JPG","page":"San Martín de los Andes","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:CPCpanoramica2.JPG","credit":"Aleposta","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Bariloche","place":"San Carlos de Bariloche, Argentina","at":[-41.1335,-71.3101],"text":"The last Argentine town before crossing the Andes into Chile.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/View_from_the_Golf_course_at_Llao_Llao.jpg/500px-View_from_the_Golf_course_at_Llao_Llao.jpg","page":"Nahuel Huapi Lake","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:View_from_the_Golf_course_at_Llao_Llao.jpg","credit":"David","license":"CC BY 2.0"}},{"name":"Osorno","place":"Osorno, Chile","at":[-40.5737,-73.1358],"text":"Across the lakes by boat into Chile, mid-February 1952.","by":"boat","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Lago_Todos_los_Santos%2C_X_Regi%C3%B3n_de_Los_Lagos%2C_Chile.jpg/500px-Lago_Todos_los_Santos%2C_X_Regi%C3%B3n_de_Los_Lagos%2C_Chile.jpg","page":"Todos los Santos Lake","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lago_Todos_los_Santos%2C_X_Regi%C3%B3n_de_Los_Lagos%2C_Chile.jpg","credit":"CARLOS TEIXIDOR CADENAS","license":"CC BY 4.0"}},{"name":"Temuco","place":"Temuco, Chile","at":[-38.7359,-72.5905],"text":"A local paper wrote them up as leprosy experts; the clipping earned meals for weeks.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Vista_Temuco.jpg/500px-Vista_Temuco.jpg","page":"Temuco","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vista_Temuco.jpg","credit":"Héctor Montero","license":"CC BY-SA 2.0"}},{"name":"Los Ángeles","place":"Los Ángeles, Chile","at":[-37.4707,-72.3517],"text":"The Norton was failing; one breakdown after another.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Vista_desde_cerro_curamavida_%283_km_a_las_afueras_de_la_ciudad%29.jpg/500px-Vista_desde_cerro_curamavida_%283_km_a_las_afueras_de_la_ciudad%29.jpg","page":"Los Ángeles, Chile","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vista_desde_cerro_curamavida_%283_km_a_las_afueras_de_la_ciudad%29.jpg","credit":"Ignaciusvilla","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Santiago","place":"Santiago, Chile","at":[-33.4377,-70.6511],"text":"La Poderosa was finally given up. From here on: hitching, trucks and boats.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Palacio_de_La_Moneda_-_miguelreflex.jpg/500px-Palacio_de_La_Moneda_-_miguelreflex.jpg","page":"Santiago","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Palacio_de_La_Moneda_-_miguelreflex.jpg","credit":"Miguel hernandez","license":"CC BY-SA 2.0"}},{"name":"Valparaíso","place":"Valparaíso, Chile","at":[-33.0458,-71.6197],"text":"The port city on its hills, and the poverty in its lower streets.","by":"truck","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Historic_Quarter_of_the_Seaport_City_of_Valpara%C3%ADso_04.jpg/500px-Historic_Quarter_of_the_Seaport_City_of_Valpara%C3%ADso_04.jpg","page":"Valparaíso","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Historic_Quarter_of_the_Seaport_City_of_Valpara%C3%ADso_04.jpg","credit":"Julia Sumangil","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Antofagasta","place":"Antofagasta, Chile","at":[-23.6464,-70.398],"text":"North as stowaways on a cargo ship, working their passage once discovered.","by":"boat","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Montaje_de_Antofagasta.jpg/500px-Montaje_de_Antofagasta.jpg","page":"Antofagasta","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Montaje_de_Antofagasta.jpg","credit":"Montaje realizado por Açipni-Lovrij.","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Chuquicamata","place":"Chuquicamata, Chile","at":[-22.3171,-68.9303],"text":"The vast copper mine in the Atacama, and the miners who worked it.","by":"truck","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Calles_de_Ayquina.jpg/500px-Calles_de_Ayquina.jpg","page":"Calama, Chile","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Calles_de_Ayquina.jpg","credit":"Carrie.g11","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}},{"name":"Arica","place":"Arica, Chile","at":[-18.4785,-70.3211],"text":"North through the desert to the Peruvian border.","by":"truck"},{"name":"Puno","place":"Puno, Peru","at":[-15.8407,-70.0284],"text":"Up onto the altiplano on trucks, beside Lake Titicaca.","by":"truck","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Lake_Titicaca_ESA22522896.jpeg/500px-Lake_Titicaca_ESA22522896.jpeg","page":"Lake Titicaca","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lake_Titicaca_ESA22522896.jpeg","credit":"European Space Agency","license":"Attribution"}},{"name":"Cusco","place":"Cusco, Peru","at":[-12.5,-72.5],"text":"The Inca capital and its Spanish churches built on Inca walls.","by":"truck","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Vista_Calle_Suecia.jpg/500px-Vista_Calle_Suecia.jpg","page":"Cusco","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vista_Calle_Suecia.jpg","credit":"tomscoffin","license":"CC BY 2.0"}},{"name":"Machu Picchu","place":"Machu Picchu, Peru","at":[-13.1643,-72.545],"text":"The lost city above the Urubamba: a high point of the journey.","by":"train","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Machu_Picchu%2C_2023_%28012%29.jpg/500px-Machu_Picchu%2C_2023_%28012%29.jpg","page":"Machu Picchu","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Machu_Picchu%2C_2023_%28012%29.jpg","credit":"Draceane","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Abancay","place":"Abancay, Peru","at":[-13.6373,-72.8789],"text":"Back across the Andes towards Lima.","by":"truck","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Plaza_de_Armas_de_Abancay.JPG/500px-Plaza_de_Armas_de_Abancay.JPG","page":"Abancay","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Plaza_de_Armas_de_Abancay.JPG","credit":"Vcardenas","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}},{"name":"Lima","place":"Lima, Peru","at":[-12.046,-77.0306],"text":"Weeks with Dr Hugo Pesce, the leprosy specialist who sent them on to the Amazon.","by":"truck","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Bas%C3%ADlica_Catedral_Metropolitana_de_Lima_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Bas%C3%ADlica_Catedral_Metropolitana_de_Lima_%28cropped%29.jpg","page":"Lima","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bas%C3%ADlica_Catedral_Metropolitana_de_Lima_%28cropped%29.jpg","credit":"David Felipe Ruiz Hoyos","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Pucallpa","place":"Pucallpa, Peru","at":[-8.3821,-74.5388],"text":"Over the mountains to the edge of the jungle.","by":"truck","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Catedral_de_la_Inmaculada_Concepci%C3%B3n-Pucallpa.jpg/500px-Catedral_de_la_Inmaculada_Concepci%C3%B3n-Pucallpa.jpg","page":"Pucallpa","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Catedral_de_la_Inmaculada_Concepci%C3%B3n-Pucallpa.jpg","credit":"EdsonFuentesMera","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Iquitos","place":"Iquitos, Peru","at":[-3.7494,-73.2444],"text":"Down the Ucayali by river boat to the Amazon.","by":"boat","photo":{"url":